; error: 6:7: 'f' changes what its first value reaches, so it can't be given what fixed 'xs' owns; give it a copy, 'xs.copy() at r', in a region the task takes, as in 'r: region', or take 'xs' as 'flex xs'
; A plain parameter is fixed, so a task can't give what it holds to a task value
; that changes what its value reaches.

task apply(f: (flex [int]@r) -> nothing, xs: [int]@r)
    f(xs)
fi
task main()
fi
